  "body_text": null,
  "page": null,
  "source": "[n_ \\.natural.+./ m_]\nDefines: n_ + m_ is \\binary.operation:on{\\naturals.set}\nexpresses:\n. piecewise:\n  if: n_ = 0\n  then: n_ + m_ := m_\n  else:\n  . let:\n    . k is \\natural\n    . n_ := \\natural.succ(k)\n    then: n_ + m_ := \\natural.succ(n_ + k)\nDocumented:\n. written: \"n_? + m_?\"\n. description: \"Addition of natural numbers, defined by recursion: $0 + m = m$,\n                and the sum with a successor is the successor of the sum. This\n                recursive definition determines $n + m$ for all naturals and\n                underlies the properties of arithmetic.\"\nId: \"5fd063d9-a3bd-4549-b060-259a727afab2\"",
